  {system: "hnswlib", url: "https://github.com/nmslib/hnswlib", overlap: "Ships incremental HNSW with M/ef_construction/ef and heuristic neighbor pruning; no evidence it implements per-item false-negative auditing, density-controlled in-degree law, or low-in-degree repair."},
  {system: "Faiss IndexHNSW", url: "https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss/blob/main/faiss/IndexHNSW.h", overlap: "Ships HNSW link structure, shrink/link routines, and singleton linking; overlap is underlying graph ANN machinery, not the claimed per-item FN mechanism."},
  {system: "Qdrant HNSW", url: "https://github.com/qdrant/qdrant/blob/master/lib/segment/src/index/hnsw_index/hnsw.rs", overlap: "Ships HNSW with heuristic graph construction and safeguards against disconnected components; no evidence of per-item FN prediction by reverse-kNN in-degree."},
  {system: "vLLM/SGLang/LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm ; https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang ; https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache ; https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer ; https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM", overlap: "Search found LLM serving/cache/kernel systems, not a shipping implementation of this graph-ANN blind-spot mechanism."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: "Not yet realistic enough for green. Evidence is N=4000, d=12, synthetic GMM, pure-Python single-layer NSW, ef_search=k=10 chosen because ef=32 made FN variance vanish. Production HNSW systems usually use multi-layer indexes, larger N, higher-dimensional embeddings, tuned ef, deletions/filters/quantization, and batch/concurrent workloads. The surviving population law has modest effect size, partial Spearman=-0.152 CI[-0.203,-0.097], but blind-spot identity stability failed at mean Spearman=0.134 < pre-registered 0.30. Reproducibility is decent for L0 because seeds, generator, graph parameters, oracle, and outcome thresholds are specified, but artifact realism is incomplete."
RATIONALE: "YELLOW: no shipping OSS system found that already implements the claimed density-controlled reverse-kNN in-degree -> per-item FN law or repair loop; existing hnswlib/Faiss/Qdrant cover the base HNSW/RNG-pruned graph machinery only. The packet's confirmed half is a systems insight if it survives real indexes: CI excludes 0 after density control and the sign is negative in all 4 density quartiles. But the original actionable per-item diagnostic is undercut because stable subset identity fails across insertion-order seeds, so current payoff is aggregate understanding/possible build-level repair, not reliable item-level triage. Prior work cited in packet also occupies nearby space: 2405.17813 studies aggregate recall vs ordering/intrinsic dimensionality, 2412.01940 studies hubs for HNSW speed (https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.01940), 2510.22316 studies query-side hardness/reachability (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.22316), and Aumuller fairness work concerns exact-search FNs (https://sigmodrecord.org/publications/sigmodRecord/2103/pdfs/12_fnn-aumuller.pdf). Advance to L1 only if tested on faiss/hnswlib at SIFT1M or real embeddings with production ef and a fixed-ef repair experiment."
